       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. That is about five times the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (some labeling allows up to 3,000 mg/day). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard tablet strength\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If 4250 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that."
