       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis. No indication supports a dose that high, and a single 4250 mg dose is far beyond any tablet strength or labeled dosing. I'd be knowingly placing an order likely to harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within labeled limits**, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or a clinical decision support override** if you have a specific reason I don't know about. Those channels can verify the order independently.\n- **Help with the clinical goal.** If you're trying to get better glycemic control, I can help enter a second agent instead of escalating metformin.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
